This file instructs Git to ignore temporary files, virtual environments, cache directories, and large video test files in order to keep your repository clean and compact.

## 📝 .gitignore
Create a file called exactly **```unset
.gitignore
```** (remember that it needs to start with a dot and not have an extension such as `.txt`) and paste the following code:

```text
# Byte-compiled / optimized / DLL files
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# C extensions
*.so

# Distribution / packaging
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg

# Virtual Environments (Highly recommended to ignore)
.venv/
venv/
ENV/
env/
育env/

# IDEs and Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Project specific media files (keeps heavy files off GitHub)
*.mp4
*.avi
*.mov
*.mkv
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
```

## 🛠️ Summary of What This Does

| Category | Ignored Items | Reason |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Python Cache** | `__pycache__/`, `*.pyc` | Generated automatically by Python and slows down Git commit process. |
| **Environments** | `.venv/`, `venv/` | Keeps local copies of installed libraries. Users are supposed to install using `requirements.txt`. |
| **Media Files** | `*.mp4`, `*.png`, etc.